lowers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashelleyPurdue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashelleyPurdue/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashelleyPurdue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashelleyPurdue/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashelleyPurdue/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashelleyPurdue/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashelleyPurdue/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ashelleyPurdue/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-21T12:43:59Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T12:47:40Z","body":"To clarify: I didn't share the .godot folder between my laptop and my desktop.  I normally _do_ have it .gitignored when using Godot normally.  I removed it from the gitignore _after_ I saw this error so I could systematically delete and revert files from it to determine which file was the culprit.  If I didn't save some kind of backup of the folder, I would potentially permanently lose the ability to reproduce the bug.\n\n> This seems to be handling the issue properly and gracefully by printing an error, if it can't find the script it can't use it\n\nThe issue is that it shouldn't have gotten into a state like this in the first place.  Normal usage of godot should not produce a .godot folder that causes this error message, and yet it did.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3426420364/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3426449802","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111829#issuecomment-3426449802","issue_url":"https://api